{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS7mHusqEoRKj7qNSZk7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the baseline. Let me review the directory structure and summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment model with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-26` — Repository with save, findById, existsById, findAll methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — POST /shipments creates shipments in CREATED status\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` — GET /shipments/{id} with ResourceNotFoundException\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) pattern\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — Converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with codes for shipment operations\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Existing tests covering create, get, list, error cases\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses for error handling, not return ResponseEntity\n- ConflictException (409) for state conflicts and duplicates\n- ResourceNotFoundException (404) for missing resources\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts all ApiExceptions to consistent ApiError envelope with `{ error: { code, message, fields } }`\n- Error codes are defined centrally in ErrorCode enum\n- No Service layer; business logic in controllers\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on error responses\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add error code for \"shipment cancelled\" conflict (necessary for feature)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for confirm endpoint scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding error code to shared ApiError.kt file (mitigated: necessary for the feature, precedent exists)\n- State transition logic correctness (mitigated: simple state machine, covered by tests)\n- Idempotency requirement must be correctly implemented (mitigated: test for retry scenario)\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Should the CANCELLED error use a new error code? Yes — consistent with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS pattern, and necessary to distinguish this error from validation failures.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This distinguishes the conflict of attempting to confirm a cancelled shipment from other validation failures.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add `confirm` endpoint method:\n   - `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Find shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return 200 with unchanged shipment (idempotency)\n   - If status is CREATED, update status to CONFIRMED, save, return 200\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with error code (409)\n   - Return ResponseEntity with status 200 and shipment body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment` — POST confirms CREATED → CONFIRMED (200, updated)\n   - `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment` — POST confirms CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED unchanged (200, same)\n   - `reject confirm on CANCELLED shipment with conflict` — POST confirms CANCELLED → 409 ConflictException\n   - `reject confirm on unknown shipment` — POST confirms non-existent → 404 ResourceNotFoundException\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered whether to use an existing error code (VALIDATION_FAILED) instead of adding a new one. Rejected because: (1) the shipment exists and the request is well-formed; this is not a validation failure, it's a state conflict; (2) consistent with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS pattern for conflicts; (3) clients need a specific code to know the state is CANCELLED, not that validation failed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Success case (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n  - Read: Shipment found by ID, status == CREATED\n  - Write: Shipment saved with status CONFIRMED\n  - Return: 200 with Shipment JSON body\n\n- **Idempotent case (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED):**\n  - Read: Shipment found by ID, status == CONFIRMED\n  - Write: None (no change)\n  - Return: 200 with unchanged Shipment JSON body\n\n- **Error case (CANCELLED):**\n  - Read: Shipment found by ID, status == CANCELLED\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: GlobalExceptionHandler converts ConflictException → 409 with error envelope `{ error: { code: \"SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\", message: \"...\" } }`\n\n- **Error case (not found):**\n  - Read: Shipment not found\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: GlobalExceptionHandler converts ResourceNotFoundException → 404 with error envelope `{ error: { code: \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", message: \"...\" } }`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test happy path: CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED with correct response\n2. Test idempotency: confirm twice, second succeeds with unchanged data\n3. Test error: CANCELLED shipment rejects with 409 and correct error code\n4. Test 404: non-existent shipment rejects with 404\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3145,"cache_read_input_tokens":22089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3145},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eba6177e-5c9c-4234-8486-b99d174cf580","uuid":"3d41a8e5-7841-4edf-a41f-6d91d7cdef5d","timestamp":"2026-09-26T13:19:31.066Z","request_id":"req_011CfS7mHRre6nbLQg8PkSbj"}
